you get to be excused from training the next morning.

51
00:04:45,240 --> 00:04:53,120
Give it to me!

52
00:04:53,120 --> 00:05:06,200
We sure haven't been seeing any demons lately, have we?

53
00:05:06,940 --> 00:05:09,660
That fact alone is enough to make my skin crawl.

54
00:05:10,440 --> 00:05:14,420
Get this. I hear it's because the demons are searching for a girl named Nezuko.

55
00:05:15,800 --> 00:05:17,740
That's just speculation, isn't it?

56
00:05:19,000 --> 00:05:21,960
It's not like anyone actually asked a demon in person.

57
00:05:21,960 --> 00:05:24,360
Well, yeah, that's true.

58
00:05:25,300 --> 00:05:29,120
But wouldn't it be great if they were gone and it was like this forever?

59
00:05:29,500 --> 00:05:31,140
That's probably wishful thinking.

60
00:05:32,020 --> 00:05:35,080
I mean, demon slaying has been going on for a thousand years now.

61
00:05:39,520 --> 00:05:42,200
Hey, where'd you go?

62
00:05:51,960 --> 00:05:58,120
Who knows? One could pop up like this any moment.

63
00:05:58,780 --> 00:06:00,160
Don't be such a jerk!

64
00:06:00,500 --> 00:06:01,920
Sorry. My bad.

65
00:06:11,300 --> 00:06:12,540
Hey, enough is enough, okay?

66
00:06:13,080 --> 00:06:14,520
We have to stay focused.

67
00:06:14,900 --> 00:06:15,300
Okay.

68
00:06:15,300 --> 00:06:21,380
Right!

69
00:06:21,380 --> 00:06:40,700
Time for the next drill!

70
00:06:41,080 --> 00:06:42,320
Split up into pairs!

71
00:06:42,320 --> 00:06:44,880
Here I go!

72
00:06:46,920 --> 00:06:48,280
So fast!

73
00:06:50,660 --> 00:06:51,920
Come on now!

74
00:06:52,240 --> 00:06:54,160
Show me what you're made of, damn it!

75
00:06:54,160 --> 00:07:10,280
So there's no way you can fight an upper rank unless you have stamina like that?

76
00:07:15,920 --> 00:07:18,760
Those upper ranks are insanely strong, right?

77
00:07:19,420 --> 00:07:21,500
You wouldn't believe the stuff they can do.

78
00:07:21,500 --> 00:07:23,180
But what was it like?

79
00:07:24,460 --> 00:07:25,520
Well, let's see.

80
00:07:26,440 --> 00:07:28,880
There'd be a pow and you'd already be hit.

81
00:07:29,500 --> 00:07:33,040
But the fact that you're not dead means you could respond in time to turn around,

82
00:07:33,400 --> 00:07:35,380
only to get slammed by them again!

83
00:07:35,720 --> 00:07:37,400
Then you feel a big crunch!

84
00:07:37,940 --> 00:07:40,220
And if that cuts off the oxygen to your brain...

85
00:07:40,220 --> 00:07:41,280
All right, that's enough.

86
00:07:41,420 --> 00:07:42,260
I think we get it.

87
00:07:42,840 --> 00:07:46,800
Sounds like it's a world far beyond the comprehension of us ordinary folks.

88
00:07:46,800 --> 00:07:51,740
All right!

89
00:07:51,740 --> 00:07:55,340
To wrap things up for today, let me see.

90
00:07:56,480 --> 00:07:57,840
You're hitting that mountain!

91
