What?

93
00:08:01,720 --> 00:08:04,140
If you don't get a move on, you're not gonna eat!

94
00:08:05,780 --> 00:08:08,720
Come on, guys, run like you mean it!

95
00:08:08,860 --> 00:08:12,100
If you can't even take this, you're not gonna cut it!

96
00:08:12,100 --> 00:08:15,100
He means well.

97
00:08:15,440 --> 00:08:17,100
Lord Tengen has a way with words.

98
00:08:17,620 --> 00:08:18,520
Sure does.

99
00:08:18,700 --> 00:08:20,340
But he's actually a softie.

100
00:08:20,760 --> 00:08:24,020
Just the other day, he refused to even eat his meal.

101
00:08:24,400 --> 00:08:25,880
Until the last slayer came back.

102
00:08:26,220 --> 00:08:28,520
In the end, he went all the way to the mountain to get him.

103
00:08:30,900 --> 00:08:32,800
You know I heard all of that, right?

104
00:08:32,800 --> 00:08:39,980
The Master put these swordsmen in my care, so I'm not about to let them burn out under my watch.

105
00:08:40,300 --> 00:08:41,380
Of course not!

106
00:08:43,260 --> 00:08:44,580
I'll be heading out then!

107
00:08:44,940 --> 00:08:45,560
Sounds good.

108
00:08:45,720 --> 00:08:46,840
That'll get you warmed up.

109
00:08:52,760 --> 00:08:57,360
Everyone with the potential to become a Hashira is kind deep down inside!

110
00:08:57,360 --> 00:09:03,420
Excuse me, can I have another tray, please?

111
00:09:03,740 --> 00:09:04,560
You got it!

112
00:09:05,440 --> 00:09:09,000
I can't take much more of this, but I've got to win!

113
00:09:10,040 --> 00:09:12,640
Or I won't be able to keep my promise to the Master!

114
00:09:15,040 --> 00:09:19,940
I've got to do all I can to keep pushing forward, so Mr. Giyu will join us!

115
00:09:21,820 --> 00:09:22,900
Can I get another?

116
00:09:23,840 --> 00:09:24,860
You got it!

117
00:09:24,860 --> 00:09:30,700
So if I lose, I have to agree to come back and take part in the training, right?

118
00:09:31,480 --> 00:09:33,660
But does that mean I don't have to if I win?

119
00:09:34,360 --> 00:09:34,800
What?

120
00:09:35,820 --> 00:09:37,820
Well, that's not...

121
00:09:37,820 --> 00:09:38,860
Here you go!

122
00:09:39,380 --> 00:09:40,480
One for you too!

123
00:09:41,640 --> 00:09:42,040
Mr.

124
00:09:42,800 --> 00:09:44,060
Please bring him another one.

125
00:09:44,320 --> 00:09:45,120
Will do!

126
00:09:47,620 --> 00:09:50,360
After this tray, I'm calling it quits.

127
00:09:50,360 --> 00:09:56,660
Meaning, if you eat that extra order of noodles, you'll have defeated me in this battle.

128
00:09:57,660 --> 00:10:02,700
And if I take part in the Hashira training after that, you'll be satisfied then, right?

129
00:10:03,560 --> 00:10:04,020
Yes!

130
00:10:04,280 --> 00:10:05,020
Very much!

131
00:10:06,020 --> 00:10:06,740
All right.

132
00:10:06,880 --> 00:10:07,880
Then finish your noodles.

133
00:10:08,580 --> 00:10:09,060
Right!

134
00:10:09,060 --> 00:10:13,940
Mr. Giyu, I'm sure that you could go on eating.

135
00:10:16,680 --> 00:10:21,960
Even so, I feel like I'm about to burst any second now!

136
00:10:21,960 --> 00:10:41,720
Sorry I'm a bit late.

137
00:10:42,580 --> 00:10:44,620
Well, I only just got here myself.

138
00:10:45,460 --> 00:10:47,660
So then, how goes the training?

139
00:10:48,660 --> 00:10:53,560
Never in a million years could I see them becoming assets in a fight against an upper rank.

140
00:10:56,280 --> 00:10:58,520
Yeah, you could say the same thing about mine.

141
00:10:59,480 --> 00:11:03,520
However, training all the core members is what the Master has asked of us.

142
00:11:04,520 --> 00:11:05,000
Yeah.

143
00:11:06,280 --> 00:11:08,780
So, what is it you wanted at this hour?

144
00:11:08,780 --> 00:11:12,080
It's just...

145
00:11:12,080 --> 00:11:13,620
It's been bugging me all this time.

146
00:11:15,000 --> 00:11:17,340
You mean what happened back at that castle?

147
00:11:20,500 --> 00:11:23,100
You and I drove the demons to the brink together.

148
00:11:23,500 --> 00:11:27,860
But just before we dispatched them, they were able to vanish in the blink of an eye.

149
00:11:31,480 --> 00:11:36,740
That many disappearing so quickly is certainly something worth at least looking into.

150
00:11:37,320 --> 00:11:37,720
Yeah.

151
00:11:38,780 --> 00:11:41,660
I've been pondering that myself since then.

152
00:11:42,180 --> 00:11:44,900
What could be behind that door that shut on us?

153
00:11:45,680 --> 00:11:50,700
That there might actually be a demon hideout that we still don't know about.

154
00:11:51,440 --> 00:11:52,700
A demon hideout, huh?

155
00:11:53,400 --> 00:11:58,460
I've been back to that castle several times since then, only to come up empty every time.

156
00:11:59,340 --> 00:12:04,420
It was right around then that demons suddenly vanished from the cities all at once.

157
00:12:04,420 --> 00:12:08,080
So what they're after is Komodo's kid sister.

158
00:12:08,080 --> 00:12:11,480
I have no doubt in my mind that's the case.

159
00:12:11,960 --> 00:12:15,440
Which leads me to believe something big is about to happen soon.

160
00:12:16,780 --> 00:12:17,100
Huh.

161
00:12:18,040 --> 00:12:22,320
Well, whenever that starts, I'll be happy to bring it all to an end.

162
00:12:22,320 --> 00:12:28,700
Don't you think this might be a bad omen for everyone here in the Demon Slayer Corps?

163
00:12:28,700 --> 00:12:35,500
So long as I'm training the Corps members, it keeps me distracted from it all.

164
00:12:35,500 --> 00:12:43,100
But I look at the situation with a dispassionate eye, and I can't help but be aware of the inevitable battle that's to come.

165
00:12:43,100 --> 00:12:52,300
That this calm we're experiencing might be the harbinger of a storm like no other.

166
00:12:53,680 --> 00:12:56,220
Worrying about it isn't going to get us anywhere, though.

167
00:12:57,360 --> 00:13:00,500
While I have you here, I do have a proposal for you.

168
00:13:01,080 --> 00:13:01,460
Heh.

169
00:13:02,460 --> 00:13:04,780
Well, I happen to have one for you, too.

170
00:13:05,220 --> 00:13:07,200
Let me go ahead and tell you mine first.

171
00:13:09,720 --> 00:13:11,420
Take me on in a match, Higuro!

172
00:13:11,420 --> 00:13:13,720
What a coincidence.

173
00:13:14,340 --> 00:13:16,840
That's exactly what I was going to propose to you.

174
00:13:21,520 --> 00:13:22,900
I'm leaving it here, alright?

175
00:13:23,280 --> 00:13:24,540
Oh, thanks, Tanjiro.

176
00:13:24,800 --> 00:13:25,540
That's perfect.

177
00:13:26,260 --> 00:13:27,440
Here, drink this.

178
00:13:28,180 --> 00:13:29,860
It's high-quality gyokuro tea.

179
00:13:30,220 --> 00:13:32,000
It helps with recovering from fatigue.

180
00:13:32,260 --> 00:13:32,760
Really?

181
00:13:33,540 --> 00:13:34,800
Don't mind if I do.

182
00:13:38,640 --> 00:13:39,240
Delicious.

183
00:13:40,300 --> 00:13:41,180
Listen, Tanjiro.

184
00:13:41,740 --> 00:13:44,460
We've been wanting to thank you for what you did at the Entertainment District.

185
00:13:44,840 --> 00:13:45,900
Thank you so much!

186
00:13:46,140 --> 00:13:46,460
Huh?

187
00:13:46,840 --> 00:13:48,120
We're extremely grateful.

188
00:13:48,580 --> 00:13:49,840
Oh, but...

189
00:13:49,840 --> 00:13:52,000
It wasn't just me, so I don't deserve it.

190
00:13:52,000 --> 00:13:55,040
Right, it was you and your younger sister.

191
00:13:55,420 --> 00:13:58,100
That boar-headed kid and the young man with the yellow hair.

192
00:13:58,740 --> 00:14:00,220
And of course, Lord Tengen.

193
00:14:00,720 --> 00:14:05,580
If even one of you hadn't been there, I don't think we could have seen the sunrise that morning.

194
00:14:06,260 --> 00:14:09,420
For Lord Tengen and all three of us to have made it back alive.

195
00:14:09,420 --> 00:14:12,200
When it seemed impossible at one point.

196
00:14:12,200 --> 00:14:14,420
It almost had to be a miracle.

197
00:14:14,420 --> 00:14:15,040
Well...

198
00:14:15,040 --> 00:14:16,800
Not, Zoro.

199
00:14:17,800 --> 00:14:18,460
But...

200
00:14:18,460 --> 00:14:21,340
The truth is, Lord Tengen still wants to keep fighting.

201
00:14:22,880 --> 00:14:23,680
She's right.

202
00:14:24,080 --> 00:14:25,580
He even calls out in his sleep.

203
00:14:26,660 --> 00:14:28,840
He's been blaming himself...

204
00:14:28,840 --> 00:14:29,800
For leaving the core.

205
00:14:31,260 --> 00:14:32,620
Tanjiro...

206
00:14:32,620 --> 00:14:34,660
Please defeat Muzanki, Butsuji.

207
00:14:36,520 --> 00:14:37,160
Right.

208
00:14:37,580 --> 00:14:38,300
I will.

209
00:14:44,520 --> 00:14:45,960
All right, everybody.

210
00:14:46,360 --> 00:14:47,140
Listen up!

211
00:14:47,740 --> 00:14:51,960
Today, I'm calling off the long-distance mountain run that we usually finish up with.

212
00:14:52,620 --> 00:14:56,420
In its place will be a special drill close to actual combat!

213
00:14:57,960 --> 00:14:59,340
To the mountain!

214
00:15:02,620 --> 00:15:05,880
Battles with demons always happen at night.

215
00:15:06,620 --> 00:15:10,480
Which is precisely why we have to hone our combat skills in the darkness.

216
00:15:11,760 --> 00:15:13,500
Strain to see in the dark.

217
00:15:13,880 --> 00:15:16,440
And what you can't see, you'll just have to sense.

218
00:15:17,220 --> 00:15:19,280
Starting now, I'm an enemy demon.

219
00:15:19,780 --> 00:15:22,100
A demon that's going to devour you.

220
00:15:23,340 --> 00:15:25,620
Let's see you try to survive.

221
00:15:26,720 --> 00:15:30,680
And, Komodo, it's your job to be the one who brings me down.

222
00:15:30,680 --> 00:15:33,540
While protecting the rest of these guys.

223
00:15:45,840 --> 00:15:47,140
Hey! Watch out!

224
00:15:47,500 --> 00:15:48,040
He's nearby!

225
00:15:48,040 --> 00:16:03,020
I can't see a thing!

226
00:16:03,780 --> 00:16:05,500
Mr. Uzui's a former shinobi.

227
00:16:06,480 --> 00:16:08,500
So I can't search for his presence by smell.

228
00:16:09,400 --> 00:16:10,000
Where is he?

229
00:16:10,460 --> 00:16:11,540
Where's Mr. Uzui?

230
00:16:11,540 --> 00:16:26,440
Mr. Uzui!

231
00:16:27,440 --> 00:16:28,360
I-impossible!

232
00:16:29,680 --> 00:16:32,060
We don't stand a chance against the Hashira!

233
00:16:35,260 --> 00:16:37,860
Would you say something like that to a demon?

234
00:16:37,860 --> 00:16:46,820
Mr. Uzui is a former Hashira, so we can't be reckless!

235
00:16:47,240 --> 00:16:48,660
We need to have a strategy!

236
00:16:49,420 --> 00:16:50,100
Stay together!

237
00:16:50,680 --> 00:16:52,020
Try and stay close to me!

238
00:16:52,480 --> 00:16:53,440
Stand back to back!

239
00:16:53,760 --> 00:16:55,200
And don't leave yourselves open!

240
00:16:56,660 --> 00:16:57,880
You're too slow!

241
00:16:58,180 --> 00:16:58,680
Slow!

242
00:16:58,680 --> 00:16:58,740
Slow!

243
00:16:58,740 --> 00:16:58,800
Slow!

244
00:17:03,800 --> 00:17:05,740
Not too shabby, Komodo.

245
00:17:05,740 --> 00:17:08,800
This strength with just one hand!

246
00:17:09,460 --> 00:17:10,360
He's incredible!

247
00:17:13,240 --> 00:17:14,720
Don't stop there now!

248
00:17:14,960 --> 00:17:16,000
Come at me again!

249
00:17:16,300 --> 00:17:16,700
Right!

250
00:17:21,640 --> 00:17:22,200
Whoa!

251
00:17:22,520 --> 00:17:23,420
They're incredible!

252
00:17:24,540 --> 00:17:27,960
He's managing to hold his own against a former Hashira!

253
00:17:27,960 --> 00:17:37,860
This is an exchange of blows between two people who fought upper ranks and survived!

254
00:17:41,360 --> 00:17:43,760
Your skills have improved, Komodo.

255
00:17:44,280 --> 00:17:45,220
Good work.

256
00:17:45,220 --> 00:18:01,020
You guys!

257
00:18:05,020 --> 00:18:05,240
Ha!

258
00:18:05,620 --> 00:18:08,380
Now you're starting to fight like demon slayers!

259
00:18:09,020 --> 00:18:09,940
Come on!

260
00:18:09,940 --> 00:18:30,380
There's no reason a retired guy like me should be clobbering you like this.

261
00:18:30,380 --> 00:18:32,380
Geez.

262
00:18:33,500 --> 00:18:34,960
Show a little bravado, huh?

263
00:18:35,700 --> 00:18:37,220
We don't stand a chance against you!

264
